      "mergeID": "6a05ef698e727ac980cefd04",
      "mergedPostDetails": "- Photo 1: A tight window width, no sidebar and no hamburger menu (bug)\n\n- Photo 2: Widened a little bit, sidebar shows up, hamburger menu gets hidden (intended)\n\n- Photo 3: Narrowed, sidebar hides, hamburger menu shows up (intended)\n\nTo reproduce, increase/decrease the window/canvas width slowly/carefully in 1 px increments/decrements.\n\nI don't have exact window resolution measurements, but it's a narrow width difference that triggers the bug (1-2 px).\n\n```\n\nMicrosoft Edge 146.0.3856.97 (Official build) (64-bit) \n\nRevision 79f6730cd02cfe9f19d33d1db200bfcdea57cf21\n\nChromium version 146.0.7680.178\n\nOperating system Windows 11 Version 25H2 (Build 26200.8117)\n\nJavaScript V8 14.6.22.11\n\nUser agent Mozilla/5.0 (Windows NT 10.0; Win64; x64) AppleWebKit/537.36 (KHTML, like Gecko) Chrome/146.0.0.0 Safari/537.36 Edg/146.0.0.0\n\nCommand-line \"C:\\Program Files (x86)\\Microsoft\\Edge\\Application\\msedge.exe\" --no-startup-window --win-session-start --flag-switches-begin --flag-switches-end\n\nExecutable path C:\\Program Files (x86)\\Microsoft\\Edge\\Application\\msedge.exe\n\n```",
